[{"text":"DiracSubstitute5[exp] rewrites \\gamma^5 in terms of the chirality projectors \\(\\gamma^6\\) and \\gamma^7. DiracSubstitute5 is also an option of various FeynCalc functions that handle Dirac algebra.","anchor":"diracsubstitute5"},{"text":"Overview, DiracSubstitute67, DiracGamma, ToDiracGamma67.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"GA[5] DiracSubstitute5[%]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^5\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^6-\\bar{\\gamma }^7\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SpinorUBar[Subscript[p, 1]] . GA[\\[Mu]] . GA[5] . GA[\\[Nu]] . SpinorU[Subscript[p, 2]] DiracSubstitute5[%]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{u}\\left(p_1\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu }.\\bar{\\gamma }^5.\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\nu }.u\\left(p_2\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\varphi (\\overline{p}_1)\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu }.\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }^6-\\bar{\\gamma }^7\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\nu }.\\left(\\varphi (\\overline{p}_2)\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"}]